## What I did

Fixed `/luxon/src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js` only (no other file touched; other agents' edits in datetime.js/duration.js/impl/util.js/interval.js left intact).

### Exact diff (`git diff -- src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js`)

```diff
diff --git a/src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js b/src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js
index 364e065..cf25d46 100644
--- a/src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js
+++ b/src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-import { formatOffset, signedOffset } from "../impl/util.js";
+import { formatOffset, signedOffset, isNumber } from "../impl/util.js";
 import Zone from "../zone.js";

 let singleton = null;
@@ -89,6 +89,6 @@ export default class FixedOffsetZone extends Zone {

   /** @override **/
   get isValid() {
-    return true;
+    return isNumber(this.fixed) && !Number.isNaN(this.fixed);
   }
 }
```

Root cause: `FixedOffsetZone#isValid` was hard-coded to `true`, so any offset (string/undefined/object/NaN) produced a "valid" zone whose `offset()` is NaN. `DateTime`'s constructor, `fromObject`, `fromJSDate`, `setZone` etc. all gate on `zone.isValid` (`!zone.isValid ? unsupportedZone(zone)`), so they now correctly produce an invalid DateTime. `isNumber` is the convention already used by `impl/util.js`; `!Number.isNaN` additionally rejects `NaN` (which `typeof` alone accepts) since a NaN offset is exactly the bug.

## Reproduction (throwaway scripts run with `npx babel-node`, deleted afterwards)

BEFORE (baseline):
- `FixedOffsetZone.instance("blorp").isValid` → `true` (expected `false`)
- `FixedOffsetZone.instance(NaN).isValid` → `true` (expected `false`)
- `FixedOffsetZone.instance(undefined).isValid` → `true`; `.instance({}).isValid` → `true`
- `DateTime.fromObject({year:2017, zone: FixedOffsetZone.instance("blorp")}).isValid` → `true`, `invalidReason` → `null` (expected `false` / `"unsupported zone"`)
- `DateTime.local().setZone(FixedOffsetZone.instance("blorp")).isValid` → `false` but `invalidReason` was `"invalid input"` (offset NaN leaked int
